{
  "_README": "DRAFT v2 (Claude, 19 Oct 2026) on Josh's tier scheme. 'level' = impact tier: 1 Minor (MDT-equivalent), 2 Moderate (widespread MDT or isolated HIGH), 3 Significant (HIGH). Major unused. Each hazard uses its own scale; 'widespread' = 6+ neighbouring ~80 km grid points (min_points). The model caps HIGH at days 1-3 and MDT at days 4-5 (MAX_CAT_BY_LEAD), so higher tiers cannot appear later. Hazards 7-9 (tropical cyclone, heatwave, snow/cold) need data not in the model run yet.",
  "scan_days": [
    1,
    7
  ],
  "neighbour_deg": 1.1,
  "_REGION_BARS": "Named thresholds that mean different things in different parts of Australia. A rule refers to one with {\"$ref_region_bar\": \"<name>\"} instead of a bare number, so a bar is tuned in ONE place rather than in every rule that uses it. 'default' is the old national number, so a region missing from by_region behaves exactly as the scan did before. Regions are defined in alerts/regions.json. FIRST PASS: these mm values come from each region's rainfall character, not from fitted climatology - there is no SILO/ERA5 percentile data in this repo yet (RULEBOOK.md section 0 makes the same admission). Replace with per-cell percentiles when pipeline/build_climatology.py grows rainfall, keeping these as the absolute floor.",
  "_RAIN_3DAY_CALIBRATION": "The rain_3day bars are calibrated, not guessed. Against the 13 alerts in alerts/issued-calibration.json, the model's single-day peak over the area Josh alerted was 25-46 mm while the 3-day total was 43-86 mm; his validity windows run 4-7 days and the titles say 'persistent'. A single-day bar low enough to see those events would be ~25 mm, which fires constantly. These bars surface 10 of 10 issued alerts that have an archived run, at ~23 events per run. Two looser sets were tested and rejected: +10 mm caught 3 of 6 heavy-rainfall alerts, +25 mm caught 1 of 6. qld_inland is 40 rather than 45 because SWPA045's 3-day total was 43 mm, and that change cost +0.7 events per run. Re-run pipeline/calibrate_against_issued.py after any change - test_regions.py fails if a change drops one of Josh's issued alerts.",
